# Environment for the Caddy container only (never the Next.js app). Production copy lives at
# /opt/codeguy/.env.caddy with mode 0600 and is not committed.
#
# Use a random password of 32+ characters from the password manager and hash it at bcrypt cost 10
# (Caddy's own `caddy hash-password` uses cost 14, about one second of shared CPU per failed
# login). Run it interactively so the password never lands in shell history:
#
#   docker run --rm -it httpd:2.4-alpine htpasswd -nBC 10 karel
#
# It prints karel:$2y$10$...; keep only the hash. Caddy accepts the $2y$ prefix.
#
# Keep the value in single quotes so Compose never interpolates the dollar signs. The deploy
# refuses a value that is not a well-formed bcrypt hash; `caddy validate` alone reliably rejects only an
# empty or missing one. A well-formed but wrong hash shows up only as failed logins.
JOBS_BASIC_AUTH_HASH='replace-with-bcrypt-hash'
